  number 11. probably one of the only  people who hated Han Solo Harrison Ford  literally begged the Creator George  Lucas to end his character after the  third film because he was fed up with  playing him and thought it would give  him some depth I did think the character  itself was relatively thin I would have  liked to see some complication for the  character the only reason he kept coming  back was because of how successful Star  Wars was so I was happy to come back and  play Han Solo again  and again but that was enough number 12.  Jason played Marshall Erickson on How I  Met Your Mother for eight years that was  part of the problem though Jason Siegel  is an incredible comedic actor he was  getting tired of Marshall's world he  thought the jokes were getting stale and  the story lines were getting predictable  also playing the same character for so  long started to weigh on his confidence  in playing other roles I didn't know if  I was a good enough actor to do it and I  kind of walked through the are you a con  man in this business kind of fear number  13. Sarah Michelle Geller hated playing  Buffy in the show's sixth season real  Buffy fans know that's when the show  took a majorly Dark Turn Sarah Michelle  Geller agrees Buffy engages in a  questionable relationship with the  soulless vampire Spike that inevitably  takes a turn into abusive territory  Geller who arguably knows Buffy better  than anyone didn't agree with her  actions that season I've always said  that season 6 was not my favorite I felt  it portrayed who she was number 14 this  Two and a Half Men star wasn't always a  fan of Jake Harper particularly after  joining a Seventh-Day Adventist Church  and converting to that religion he  couldn't find it in him to continue to  support the show he made a pretty bold  statement to People magazine I'm on Two  and a Half Men and I don't want to be on  it please stop watching it please stop  filling your head with filth number 15.  Catherine Heigl starred in one of the  most successful longest running TV shows  Gray's Anatomy though she won a prime  time Emmy in 2007 for best supporting  actress in a drama series she still  worked very hard to separate herself  from her character Izzy and the show as  a whole she even went as far as to  refuse her work for consideration of  another award the following year she  didn't think the material she had to  work with deserved an award  unsurprisingly in 2010 she ended up  leaving the show after a lot of  speculation around the topic that same  year she told USA Today I felt she was  an admirable woman who certainly made  mistakes but I was starting to not like  her and that bothered me  do you have any idea how much these  actors hated their own characters we can  definitely understand why for many of  them which character on this list is  your favorite
 

